    <imageSet>
        <name>Unaligned and compressed multi-frame micrographs</name>
        <directory>/data/01_Raw_Frames</directory>
        <category>micrographs - multiframe</category>
        <headerFormat>MRCS</headerFormat>
        <dataFormat>MRCS</dataFormat>
        <numImagesOrTiltSeries>3383</numImagesOrTiltSeries>
        <framesPerImage>80</framesPerImage>
        <frameRange>
            <frameRangeMin>1</frameRangeMin>
            <frameRangeMax>80</frameRangeMax>
        </frameRange>
        <voxelType>UNSIGNED 16 BIT INTEGER</voxelType>
        <dimensions>
            <imageWidth>3838</imageWidth>
            <pixelWidth>0.5175</pixelWidth>
            <imageHeight>3710</imageHeight>
            <pixelHeight>0.5175</pixelHeight>
        </dimensions>
        <details>Data collection was performed using a dose of ~91.56 e-/Å2 across 80 frames (75 msec per frame) at a dose rate of ~4.0 e–/pix/sec, using a set defocus range of -1.2 μm to -1.8 μm. Raw frames were compressed using pbzip2. Gain reference image to use is 18jun08i_08213559_01_3710x3838_norm_0_mod.mrc. Magnification anisotropy is present (Distortion angle of 172.7 degrees, major scale of 1.007 and minor scale of 0.993). The script to correct for magnification anisotropy (mag_distort_correct4.cs is attached, and it requires the mag_distortion_correct software available from the Grigorieff lab website.</details>
        <segmentationList/>
        <micrographsFilePattern></micrographsFilePattern>
        <pickedParticlesFilePattern></pickedParticlesFilePattern>
        <pickedParticlesDirectory></pickedParticlesDirectory>
    </imageSet>
    <imageSet>
        <name>Aligned and magnification anisotropy corrected micrographs</name>
        <directory>/data/02_Aligned_Micrographs</directory>
        <category>micrographs - single frame</category>
        <headerFormat>MRC</headerFormat>
        <dataFormat>MRC</dataFormat>
        <numImagesOrTiltSeries>3297</numImagesOrTiltSeries>
        <framesPerImage>1</framesPerImage>
        <voxelType>32 BIT FLOAT</voxelType>
        <dimensions>
            <imageWidth>3838</imageWidth>
            <pixelWidth>0.5175</pixelWidth>
            <imageHeight>3710</imageHeight>
            <pixelHeight>0.5175</pixelHeight>
        </dimensions>
        <details>Micrographs aligned using MotionCor2, magnification anisotropy corrected. Alignment was done initially using 3x3 patches (Patch3_micrographs). Micrographs that had estimated resolution at 0.5 confidence level of worse than 10 Å were removed, resulting in 3,297 micrographs. Patch2_micrographs were used later during refinement - hence only a subset of micrographs were aligned using 2x2 patches (Patch2_micrographs).</details>
        <segmentationList/>
        <micrographsFilePattern></micrographsFilePattern>
        <pickedParticlesFilePattern></pickedParticlesFilePattern>
        <pickedParticlesDirectory></pickedParticlesDirectory>
    </imageSet>
